# Use TEAM handles (@Branch8/team-name), never individual usernames.
#
# An individual owner is a single point of failure twice over: reviews stall when
# they are on leave, and their departure silently removes the required reviewer
# from every rule below. A team survives both.
#
# Each team here should have at least two members.
#
# ⚠ BEFORE THIS FILE DOES ANYTHING: the teams below must actually exist under the
# Branch8 organization on GitHub. A CODEOWNERS rule naming a non-existent team is
# not an error - GitHub silently applies no rule at all, so PRs merge with no
# required review while the file looks like it is protecting you. Create the teams
# first, then confirm on a test PR that the reviewer is auto-requested.

*                   @Branch8/platform-team

# Third-party code gets a second pair of eyes. These diffs are the whole point
# of vendoring - do not let them merge on autopilot.
/vendor/            @Branch8/platform-team @Branch8/security
/vendor.lock.json   @Branch8/platform-team @Branch8/security

# The automation itself. Whoever can change these can change what ships to
# everyone, so hold them to the same bar as the plugins.
/.github/           @Branch8/platform-team
/scripts/           @Branch8/platform-team

# The distribution list and the Claude Code managed-settings payload. Changing
# either changes what every colleague's agent loads.
/.claude-plugin/       @Branch8/platform-team
/managed-settings.json @Branch8/platform-team
